<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Solduz</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Solduz is a valley and plain in West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> province of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-urmia">Lake Urmia</a>, around the modern town of Naqadeh. It contains the mound of Hasanlu Tepe, whose fortified <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> citadel dominated the valley until its destruction around 800 BCE, and many other prehistoric sites investigated by archaeologists.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/solduz.jpg" alt="Solduz" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sina Khezrii · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Naghadeh_City.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
